ENTRY            32908   20260527   20261124   20261124       3224
SUBENT        32908001   20260527   20261124   20261124       3224
BIB                 14         47
TITLE      Direct measurement of the 103Rh(n,g) and 103Rh(g,n)
            cross section up to stellar temperatures at the CSNS
            Back-n and SSRF SLEGS
AUTHOR     (Hao Liang, Zhen-Dong An, Wei Jiang, Zi-Rui Hao,
            Chen-Chen Guo, Yu-Gang Ma, Jie Ren, Xi-Chao Ruan,
            Jing-Yu Tang, Rui-Rui Fan, Gong-Tao Fan,
            Hong-Wei Wang, Wen-Qing Shen , Yu-Bing Li,
            Jun-Heng Hu, Di Sun, Ting Liu, Zi-Jun Liu, Yi Sui)
REFERENCE  (J,PL/B,872,140105,2026)
REL-REF    (O,G0102001,Hao Liang+,J,PL/B,872,140105,2026)
            103Rh(g,n) dataset compiled separately
INSTITUTE  (3CPRIMP,3CPRSZH,3CPRFUD,3CPRIHP,3CPRARI,3CPRNRS,
            3CPRAEP,3CPRHST)
           (3CPRCPR) Spallation Neutron Source Science Center,
            Dongguan; Shenyang Normal University, Shenyang;
            University of South China, Hengyang; Guangxi Normal
            University, Guilin
FACILITY   (SYNCH,3CPRIHP) The back-streaming white neutron
            beamline (Back-n) at the China Spallation Neutron
            Source (CSNS)
INC-SOURCE (SPALL) Neutrons are produced via a 1.6 GeV pulsed
            proton beam at 25 Hz to bombard a tungsten target.
            The proton beam current was in double-bunch mode with
            a 41 ns FWHM of proton pulse width and 410 ns
            interval. A neutron energy spectrum of 0.1 eV - 400
            MeV with a flux 1E7 n/cm2/s was provided.
SAMPLE     The 103Rh sample with diameter of 30 mm, thickness of
            1 mm, density of 12.30 g/cm3, and purity of 99.95%.
DETECTOR   (SCIN) The C6D6 detectors, with low neutron
            sensitivity, use Pulse Height Weighting Technique
            (PHWT) to eliminate dependence on cascading gamma-
            ray energy. The EJ315 scintillator and
            photomultiplier tube enable a 10 ns response.
METHOD     (TOF,PHWT) The length of neutron flight path is 76 m.
ADD-RES    The Maxwellian-averaged cross sections (MACS)
            calculated using the default TALYS parameters.
ERR-ANALYS (ERR-T) Total error
           (ERR-1) Sample parameters
           (ERR-2,,8.0) Neutron spectrum below 0.15 MeV
           (ERR-3,,4.5) Neutron spectrum above 0.15 MeV
           (ERR-4,,1.5) Proton beam power
           (ERR-5) PHWT due to the C6D6 detector system
           (ERR-6) Double bunch spectrum unfolding method
           (ERR-7) Normalization
STATUS     (APRVD) Proofread by Zirui Hao and Zhen-Dong An.
HISTORY    (20251215R) Data received from Zirui Hao.
           (20250527C) Wang Jimin
ENDBIB              47
COMMON               4          3
ERR-1      ERR-5      ERR-6      ERR-7
PER-CENT   PER-CENT   PER-CENT   PER-CENT
        0.1        1.1        2.0        1.5
ENDCOMMON            3
ENDSUBENT           54
SUBENT        32908002   20260527   20261124   20261124       3224
BIB                  3          5
REACTION  1(45-RH-103(N,G)45-RH-104,,RYL)
          2(45-RH-103(N,G)45-RH-104,,SIG)
CORRECTION2Corrected for multiple scattering effect through
            GEANT4 simulations
STATUS     (TABLE,,Hao Liang+,J,PL/B,872,140105,2026)
ENDBIB               5
COMMON               1          3
THICKNESS
